---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Recognition Criteria for Intangible Assets" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Internally Generated Intangible Assets — Research and Development" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Finite-Life Intangible Assets — Amortized" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Indefinite-Life Intangible Assets — Tested for Impairment" },
        { id: "s7", label: "THE GOODWILL MEASUREMENT CHOICE — Impairment-Only or Amortization" },
        { id: "s8", label: "The Goodwill Impairment Test, Where Elected" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Amortizing an Acquired Customer List" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Worked Example — the Goodwill Impairment Test" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Relationship to IAS 38 / IFRS 3" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">





<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Intangible assets and goodwill, with a genuinely distinctive amortization alternative</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 3064 governs the RECOGNITION and MEASUREMENT of INTANGIBLE assets and GOODWILL — COVERING BOTH internally GENERATED and SEPARATELY acquired INTANGIBLE assets, and THE subsequent MEASUREMENT of GOODWILL recognized UNDER Section 1582 (see the COMPANION poster). GENUINELY distinctively, ASPE PERMITS an ENTERPRISE to ELECT to AMORTIZE goodwill OVER its ESTIMATED useful LIFE, RATHER than TESTING it EXCLUSIVELY for IMPAIRMENT (Section 7).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Identifiable non-monetary assets without physical substance, and goodwill</div><div class="principle">This Section applies to IDENTIFIABLE non-MONETARY assets WITHOUT physical SUBSTANCE (INTANGIBLE assets), and TO goodwill RECOGNIZED in a BUSINESS combination UNDER Section 1582.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Recognition Criteria for Intangible Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Identifiability, control, and probable future economic benefits</div><div class="text-supporting">AN intangible ASSET is recognized ONLY where it IS identifiable (SEPARABLE, or ARISING from CONTRACTUAL or OTHER legal RIGHTS), the ENTERPRISE controls IT, FUTURE economic BENEFITS are PROBABLE, and ITS cost CAN be RELIABLY measured.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Internally Generated Intangible Assets — Research and Development</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Research costs expensed; development costs capitalized if criteria are met</div><div class="text-supporting">RESEARCH costs are EXPENSED as INCURRED. DEVELOPMENT costs are CAPITALIZED only WHERE specific CRITERIA are MET — TECHNICAL feasibility, INTENTION and ABILITY to COMPLETE and USE or SELL the ASSET, and the ABILITY to RELIABLY measure THE attributable EXPENDITURE — CONSISTENT with the GENERAL approach ALSO used internationally UNDER IAS 38.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Finite-Life Intangible Assets — Amortized</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Systematic amortization over the useful life</div><div class="text-supporting">INTANGIBLE assets WITH a FINITE useful LIFE (e.g. a PATENT with a LEGAL expiration, a CUSTOMER list EXPECTED to GENERATE benefits OVER a SPECIFIC period) are AMORTIZED systematically OVER that USEFUL life, MUCH as an ITEM of PROPERTY, plant, AND equipment WOULD be under SECTION 3061.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Indefinite-Life Intangible Assets — Tested for Impairment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">No amortization, but subject to impairment testing</div><div class="text-supporting">INTANGIBLE assets WITH an INDEFINITE useful LIFE (RARE under ASPE, GIVEN the FRAMEWORK'S generally AMORTIZATION-oriented default) are NOT amortized, but ARE tested FOR impairment UPON indicators OF impairment ARISING, SIMILAR in SPIRIT to the GOODWILL impairment approach (Section 8).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>THE GOODWILL MEASUREMENT CHOICE — Impairment-Only or Amortization</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A genuine, private-enterprise-oriented accounting policy election</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise MAY elect, as AN accounting POLICY choice, to EITHER (a) test GOODWILL for IMPAIRMENT only UPON indicators OF impairment ARISING (RATHER than MANDATORY annual TESTING), or (b) AMORTIZE goodwill ON a straight-LINE basis OVER its ESTIMATED useful LIFE, NOT exceeding TEN years WHERE a LIFE cannot BE reliably ESTIMATED — TESTING for IMPAIRMENT only UPON indicators OF impairment ARISING under EITHER approach. THIS genuinely DISTINCTIVE alternative WAS introduced IN the Section 1582 POSTER (see the COMPANION poster) and IS repeated HERE as the FULL, ongoing SUBSEQUENT-measurement framework GOVERNING goodwill THROUGHOUT its LIFE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>The Goodwill Impairment Test, Where Elected</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Comparing the reporting unit's fair value to its carrying amount</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE the IMPAIRMENT-only approach IS elected, GOODWILL impairment is TESTED by COMPARING the FAIR value OF the REPORTING unit TO which the GOODWILL relates AGAINST that REPORTING unit'S carrying AMOUNT (INCLUDING goodwill) — WITH any EXCESS of CARRYING amount OVER fair VALUE recognized AS an IMPAIRMENT loss, LIMITED to the CARRYING amount OF goodwill ITSELF.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Amortizing an Acquired Customer List</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A finite-life intangible asset, amortized systematically</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A customer relationship intangible from an acquisition</div><div class="wk-body">A company acquires a customer list valued at $450,000 in a business combination, with an estimated 9-year useful life based on expected customer attrition patterns.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company AMORTIZES the CUSTOMER list at $450,000 ÷ 9 = <strong>$50,000 per year</strong>, ON a straight-LINE basis, CONSISTENT with the GENERAL finite-LIFE intangible ASSET amortization approach.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — the Goodwill Impairment Test</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recognizing an impairment loss, limited to goodwill's carrying amount</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A reporting unit's fair value has declined</div><div class="wk-body">A company elects the impairment-only approach for its $900,000 of goodwill. Due to a significant, sustained decline in operating performance (an impairment indicator), the reporting unit's fair value is determined to be $3,200,000, against a carrying amount (including goodwill) of $3,700,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The IMPAIRMENT loss = $3,700,000 − $3,200,000 = $500,000, LIMITED to the $900,000 CARRYING amount OF goodwill — the COMPANY recognizes a <strong>$500,000</strong> goodwill IMPAIRMENT loss, REDUCING goodwill to $400,000.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 3064 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Useful lives and amortization methods for finite-life intangible assets</span><span>Goodwill's subsequent measurement policy (impairment-only or amortization) and, if amortized, its useful life</span><span>Amount of any goodwill or intangible asset impairment loss recognized during the period</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether to elect goodwill amortization or the impairment-only approach</span><span>Whether development costs meet the specific capitalization criteria</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Useful lives of finite-life intangibles and, if elected, of goodwill</span><span>Fair value of a reporting unit, for goodwill impairment testing</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 38 / IFRS 3</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 3064 vs IAS 38 / IFRS 3</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 3064</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 38 / IFRS 3</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Development cost capitalization criteria</span><span>Same core criteria</span><span>Same core criteria — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Goodwill subsequent measurement</span><span>Impairment-only OR amortization alternative</span><span>Impairment-only ONLY</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">THE goodwill AMORTIZATION alternative REMAINS the SINGLE most SIGNIFICANT divergence FROM unmodified IFRS — INTANGIBLE asset RECOGNITION and AMORTIZATION mechanics OTHERWISE remain THOROUGHLY converged.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every goodwill/intangible event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Goodwill amortization (if elected)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Systematic straight-line expense</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Goodwill impairment (if elected)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Recognized upon indicators, limited to goodwill's carrying amount</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1582</span><span>Business Combinations — supplies the initial goodwill recognition this Section's subsequent measurement applies to</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3063</span><span>Impairment of Long-lived Assets — governs impairment testing for tangible and finite-life intangible assets, distinct from goodwill's own approach here</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Goodwill amortization alternative</div><div class="glossary-def">An accounting policy election permitting a private enterprise to amortize goodwill straight-line over its estimated useful life (up to 10 years), rather than testing exclusively for impairment.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Reporting unit</div><div class="glossary-def">The level at which goodwill is tested for impairment under the impairment-only approach.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe3064 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
